  "review": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "Messages lists/counts only live pending questions and approvals blocking human input. Selecting a request opens its owning item/run and original dialog, answering returns there and removes only that request. Nonblocking requests stay available in their conversation; stale/answered/orphaned/disconnected records are excluded from this queue.",
    "implementation": "Inspected Factory direct routing, queue filtering and Messages rows; ItemDetail read/version guards and collapsed triage; NewChat explicit prepare/start and same-run uncertainty; Agent transcript and expected-turn follow-up. GitHub.Sync adds requested users/teams and App.Sync stores authenticated viewer/team feedback; Inbox uses forward/reverse/external PR relationships. Existing bridge, isolated workspace and authority validation remain. Factory separates pending requests from the blocking live waiting queue and uses only the latter for Messages content/count; request IDs continue to drive openAttention and Answer. All agents is removed from Messages and work history is scoped to its owning item.",
    "tests": "Read UI-WORK-QUEUES, UI-DIRECT-CHAT, UI-CHAT-UNCERTAIN, UI-CHAT-AUTHORITY, UI-CHAT-CONFIRMED, UI-WAITING-MESSAGES and the updated real MCP/store/Git/fake-provider assembled first-message path. Existing independent read/New/action, narrow themes, modal keyboard, draft isolation, optional launch review and dirty cleanup/Resume assertions remain. Provider/app tests cover review-request removal without timestamps, paginated membership and permission/account changes, and bidirectional/external PR links. Scenarios without broader host/manual evidence retain stable gaps. Expanded Messages fixture mixes blocking questions/approval with nonblocking, answered, stale, orphaned and disconnected records; asserts count three, exact second-task answer ownership, exact approval decline, one remaining question, then empty queue/count hidden. Direct interrupt fixture stales old questions and refuses them after session wake."
  },
